1.WHO HAS THE MAJORITY?
Given an array arr[] and two elements x and y, return the element that occurs more frequently. 
If both elements have the same frequency, return the smaller one.
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            public int moreFrequent(List<Integer> arr, int x, int y) {
                int xcount=0;
                int ycount=0;
                for(int i=0;i<arr.size();i++){
                    if(arr.get(i)==x){
                        xcount++;
                    }
                    if(arr.get(i)==y){
                        ycount++;
                    }
                }
                if(xcount==ycount){
                    return Math.min(x,y);
                }
                return (xcount>ycount)?x:y;        
            }
        }
PROBLEM LINK : https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/who-has-the-majority/1


2.INSERTION SORT 
Given an array arr[] of positive integers.The task is to complete the insertsort() function which is used to implement Insertion Sort.
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            public void insertionSort(int arr[]) {
                for(int i=0;i<arr.length;i++){
                    int j=i;
                    while(j>0 && arr[j-1]>arr[j]){
                        int temp=arr[j-1];
                        arr[j-1]=arr[j];
                        arr[j]=temp;
                        j--;
                    }
                }
            }
        }
PROBLEM LINK : https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/insertion-sort/1?page=1&category%5B%5D=Algorithms&query=category%5B%5DAlgorithmspage1


3.SELECTION SORT 
Given an array arr, use selection sort to sort arr[] in increasing order.
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            void selectionSort(int[] arr) {
                int n=arr.length;
                for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
                    int min=i;
                    for(int j=i;j<n;j++){
                        if(arr[j]<arr[min]){
                            min=j;
                        }
                    }
                    int temp=arr[min];
                    arr[min]=arr[i];
                    arr[i]=temp; 
                }
            }
        }
PROBLEM LINK : https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/selection-sort/1


4.BUBBLE SORT 
Given an array, arr[]. Sort the array using bubble sort algorithm.
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            public void bubbleSort(int[] arr) {
                for(int i=0;i<arr.length-1;i++){
                    for(int j=0;j<arr.length-1-i;j++){
                        if(arr[j]>arr[j+1]){
                            int temp=arr[j];
                            arr[j]=arr[j+1];
                            arr[j+1]=temp;
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
PROBLEM LINK : https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/bubble-sort/1


5.MAX VALUE PERMUTATION 
Given an array arr[] of integers, rearrange its elements in any order to maximize the value of: 
Σ(arr[i] × i), where 0 ≤ i < n
Return the maximum possible value .
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            int maxValue(int arr[]) {
                Arrays.sort(arr);
                int max=0;
                for(int i=0;i<arr.length;i++){
                    max+=(arr[i]*i);
                }
                return max;
            }
        }
