8.SUM OF ALTERNATE PRODUCTS 
Given an array arr[] of even size consisting of positive integers. After sorting the array, 
find the sum of the product of i-th element from starting and i-th element from last.
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            public int altProduct(int[] arr) {
                Arrays.sort(arr);
                int n=arr.length;
                int j=n-1;
                int sum=0;
                for(int i=0;i<n/2;i++){
                    sum+=(arr[i]*arr[j]);
                    j--;
                }
                return sum;
            }
        }
PROBLEM LINK : https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/minimize-sum-of-alternate-product2033/1


9.FRIENDLY ARRAY
Numbers have a measure of friendliness defined as the absolute difference between them. 
Given an circular array of integers arr[], calculate the friendliness of the array. 
Friendliness is the sum of the absolute differences between each element and its closest friend in the array.
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            public int calculateFriendliness(int[] arr) {
                int sum=0;
                for(int i=1;i<arr.length;i++){
                    sum+=Math.abs(arr[i]-arr[i-1]);
                }
                sum+=Math.abs(arr[arr.length-1]-arr[0]);
                return sum;
            }
        }
PROBLEM LINK : https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/friendly-array2009/1


